    "abstract": "Parts breakdown of the forward primary distribution centre contactor installation, showing the original and the latching module standards as alternates together with the interface bracket used at the outboard positions.",
    "sections": {
      "purpose": "Illustrated parts breakdown of the contactor module installation in the forward primary distribution centre, covering the original standard and the latching standard as alternate items.",
      "figure_note": "The figure is drawn looking forward at the rack front face with the cover removed. Sheet 1 shows the three primary positions and sheet 2 shows the interface bracket detail at the outboard positions only. The alternates at items 10 and 20 are the two module standards: order against the aircraft configuration record, not against the position, because a mixed rack is possible on an aircraft part way through conversion. The effectivity column is now reproduced on the spares pick list generated from this figure, which it was not before; a pick list that carries only the item number and the part number cannot be resolved from the aircraft serial when two standards sit at the same item, and the orders that came back for clarification were all of that kind. The arrangement was agreed with the spares organisation. The interface bracket at item 40 is fitted at the outboard positions only and does not appear at the inboard position."
    },
